Lint Markdown files and print warnings/errors

Usage: rumdl.exe check [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...

Arguments:
  [PATHS]...
          Files or directories to check (use '-' for stdin)

Options:
  -f, --fix
          Fix issues automatically where possible

      --preflight
          Plan and validate the entire batch before applying fixes

      --diff
          Show diff of what would be fixed instead of fixing files

  -d, --disable <DISABLE>
          Disable specific rules (comma-separated)

  -e, --enable <ENABLE>
          Enable only specific rules (comma-separated)
          
          [alias: --rules]

      --extend-enable <EXTEND_ENABLE>
          Extend the list of enabled rules (additive with config)

      --extend-disable <EXTEND_DISABLE>
          Extend the list of disabled rules (additive with config)

      --no-code-block-tools
          Skip configured code-block tools while preserving all other configuration

      --only-code-block-tools
          Run only configured code-block tools, without processing the outer Markdown document

      --fixable <FIXABLE>
          Only allow these rules to be fixed (comma-separated)

      --unfixable <UNFIXABLE>
          Prevent these rules from being fixed (comma-separated)

      --exclude <EXCLUDE>
          Exclude specific files or directories (comma-separated glob patterns)

      --no-exclude
          Disable all exclude patterns

      --include <INCLUDE>
          Include only specific files or directories (comma-separated glob patterns)

      --color <COLOR>
          Control colored output
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --respect-gitignore[=<RESPECT_GITIGNORE>]
          Respect .gitignore, .ignore and git exclude files when scanning directories (.markdownlintignore always applies; neither applies to explicitly named files)
          
          [possible values: true, false]

  -c, --config <CONFIG_OPTION>
          Path to a configuration file, or an inline TOML override.
          
          May be passed multiple times. Each value is either a path to a TOML
          configuration file or an inline `KEY = VALUE` snippet that overrides
          configuration options at the highest precedence:
          
            - Rule option: `--config 'MD013.line-length = 20'`
            - Global option: `--config 'line-length = 20'`
            - Explicit global section: `--config 'global.line-length = 20'`
          
          At most one value may be a file path; the rest must be inline TOML.
          Inline overrides still apply with `--no-config` or `--isolated`, which
          reject only the file path.

  -q, --quiet
          Print diagnostics, but suppress summary lines

      --no-config
          Ignore all configuration files and use built-in defaults (--isolated is also accepted)

      --show-full-path
          Show absolute file paths in output instead of relative paths

      --stdin-filename <STDIN_FILENAME>
          Filename to use when reading from stdin (e.g., README.md)

      --stderr
          Output diagnostics to stderr instead of stdout

      --no-cache
          Disable caching (re-check all files)

      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          Directory to store cache files (default: .rumdl_cache, or $RUMDL_CACHE_DIR, or cache-dir in config)

      --deny-config-warnings
          Treat configuration warnings as errors (exit code 2)

  -v, --verbose
          Show detailed output

      --profile
          Show profiling information

      --statistics
          Show statistics summary of rule violations

      --output-format <OUTPUT_FORMAT>
          Output format for diagnostics (default: text).
          
          Precedence: --output-format > $RUMDL_OUTPUT_FORMAT > config file > text

          Possible values:
          - text:       One-line-per-warning with file, line, column, rule, and message (default)
          - full:       Show source lines with caret underlines highlighting the violation
          - concise:    Minimal: file:line:col rule message
          - grouped:    Warnings grouped by file with a header per file
          - json:       JSON array of all warnings (collected across files)
          - json-lines: One JSON object per warning (streaming)
          - github:     GitHub Actions annotation format (::warning/::error)
          - gitlab:     GitLab Code Quality report (JSON)
          - pylint:     Pylint-compatible format
          - azure:      Azure Pipelines logging commands
          - sarif:      SARIF 2.1.0 for static analysis tools
          - junit:      JUnit XML for CI test reporters

      --flavor <FLAVOR>
          Markdown flavor to use: standard (also accepts gfm/github/commonmark), mkdocs, mdx, pandoc, quarto, obsidian, kramdown, azure_devops (also accepts azure/ado), myst (also accepts mystmd), hugo (also accepts goldmark), mdg (also accepts markdown_with_gherkin), or gh-aw (preview)
          
          [possible values: standard, mkdocs, mdx, pandoc, quarto, obsidian, kramdown, azure_devops, myst, hugo, mdg, gh-aw]

      --stdin
          Read from stdin instead of files

      --stdin-batch
          Read NUL-delimited path/content pairs from stdin

      --stdin-batch-closed-world
          Resolve links only against documents supplied by --stdin-batch

      --stdin-batch-targets <FILE>
          Read NUL-terminated link target paths (not linted) from FILE; a trailing / marks a directory

  -s, --silent
          Suppress diagnostics and summaries

  -w, --watch
          Run in watch mode by re-running whenever files change

      --fail-on <FAIL_ON>
          Exit code behavior: 'any' (default) exits 1 on any violation, 'warning' on warning+error, 'error' only on errors, 'never' always exits 0

          Possible values:
          - any:     Exit 1 on any violation (info, warning, or error)
          - warning: Exit 1 on warning or error severity violations
          - error:   Exit 1 only on error-severity violations
          - never:   Always exit 0
          
          [default: any]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
